growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.41370524243620777,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.017993237754122537,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":27.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.11582,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":77.2,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Redwood Trust, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a specialty finance company in the United States. It operates through four segments: Sequoia Mortgage Banking, CoreVest Mortgage Banking, Redwood Investments, and Legacy Investments. The Residential Consumer Mortgage Banking segment operates a mortgage loan conduit that acquires residential loans from third-party originators for subsequent sale, securitization, or transfer to its investment portfolio. The CoreVest Mortgage Banking segment operates a platform that originates residential investor loans for subsequent securitization, sale, or transfer into the Redwood Investments portfolio or into joint ventures. This segment also includes various derivative financial instruments that we utilize to manage certain risks associated with our inventory of loans held for sale. The Redwood Investments segment primarily targets investments with sensitivity to housing credit risk, sourced through our operating platforms where control the underwriting and collateral review. Going forward, the Redwood Investments portfolio will focus on retained interests from the company's own securitizations and other investment vehicles, rather than third-party securities, consistent with Redwood's strategic shift toward internally originated investments. The Legacy Investments segment consists of assets no longer aligned with our core strategic objectives, including legacy unsecuritized bridge and term loans, residential re-performing loan securities, and other non-core legacy assets that are in the active process of sale, runoff, or other disposition as part of the accelerated strategic repositioning of our business model. Redwood Trust, Inc. was incorporated in 1994 and is headquartered in Mill Valley, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher J. Abate CPA | CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 351 people. Stock-based compensation of $57K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Redwood Trust, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $363M market cap.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and -5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -0% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Accruals are elevated at +42.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 41.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +42.3% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 329% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 87/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.0M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Redwood Trust (NYSE:RWT) Issues Quarterly Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/redwood-trust-nyserwt-issues-quarterly-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793905850.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.948,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","legal"]},{"title":"Director Doneene K Damon Converts 10,376 Deferred Stock Units into Redwood Trust (NYSE:RWT) Common Shares","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.